<BaseLayout
  title="About — PixelMatch Blog"
  description="The editorial blog of PixelMatch, AI product photography for Amazon, Shopify, Etsy, and TikTok Shop sellers."
>
  <h1 class="text-ink">About the PixelMatch Blog</h1>
  <div class="prose-pm max-w-prose">
    <p>
      This blog is the editorial arm of <a href="https://pixelmatch.art">PixelMatch</a> —
      an AI product photography tool built for ecommerce sellers. We
      publish step-by-step playbooks, honest tool comparisons, and
      seller case studies covering Amazon, Shopify, Etsy, and TikTok Shop.
    </p>

    <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/blog/learn/">How-to guides</a> for product photography, background removal, batch resizing, and listing-asset workflows.</li>
      <li><a href="/blog/compare/">Tool comparisons</a> — PixelMatch vs Photoroom, Canva, Pebblely, Photoroom, and other AI image generators.</li>
      <li><a href="/blog/stories/">Seller case studies</a> with real numbers, real workflows, and honest limitations.</li>
      <li><a href="/blog/policy/">Platform image policies</a> — exact pixel requirements and how to fix common listing rejections.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
    <p>
      Articles are AI-assisted and reviewed for factual accuracy against
      official platform documentation. When a specific number or policy
      can't be verified through search, we say so explicitly rather than
      guessing. Pricing, fees, and policy details change frequently —
      always cross-reference with the platform's official docs before
      acting on time-sensitive guidance.
    </p>

    <h2>Try PixelMatch</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://pixelmatch.art/signup?utm_source=blog&utm_medium=about&utm_campaign=about_page">
        Sign up free
      </a>
      and generate your first 50 product images, no credit card required.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
